[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Start "caro-panov 4...Nf6"]
[Name "Panov: 5.c5"]

5. c5 { Grabs space, and gives up all pressure on d5 to do it. }
5... Nc6 { Plain development. Now that d5 is not attacked, Black has no need of ...e6, and the bishop can come out. }
6. Nf3 Bg4 { The rule of the opening again, with the same pin as in the main line. }
7. Be2 e6 { Black has everything the opening asks for: the bishop outside, a solid centre, and an easy game. } *
